@startuml
' Evidence: Laplace-MCP/native/api.c SHA256 51ff00d86b27e74206f04c97974b8cc433e9c6d3184d88665411d55d6f17eefc
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFCFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
title Modular MCP — constituent SQL forward and shape routes
start
:Extract one input for forward, or input and other for shape;
:Name each text with up to 256 constituent slots;
:Serialize constituent IDs; reject empty or overflowing list;
:Open/reuse database connection;
if (Connection unavailable?) then (yes)
 :HTTP 503;
 stop
endif
if (Forward route?) then (yes)
 :Bind array of constituent IDs;
 :Query laplace_forward with literal 64; LIMIT 128 rows;
 :Return trunk ID, timing and aggregated observed-span rows;
else (Shape route)
 :Bind two ID lists;
 :JOIN stored entity coordinates preserving constituent ordinal;
 :Build lines; call laplace_frechet4d;
 :Return two trunk IDs, distance and timing;
endif
if (Query helper reports failure?) then (yes)
 :Attempt ROLLBACK; HTTP 500 with detail;
else (success)
 :HTTP 200;
endif
stop
footer
Source-reviewed orchestration. Nested semantics remain open; no runtime acceptance
claimed. Both handlers and their SQL strings reviewed. Forward here is the specific
laplace_forward span query, not the Engine pull program or monorepo obligation-closing
forward. Shape inner joins can omit missing constituent coordinates; q2 does not
separately reject a SQL NULL value.
end footer

@enduml
